Text: "**Mathlore** is a structured mathematical library written in the
       **Mathlingua** language. Its purpose is expository as well as formal: a
       definition should say what data are being introduced, a theorem should
       make its hypotheses visible, and the surrounding prose should explain
       why the concept is useful and how it fits into the larger theory.

       The collection follows a dependency-conscious path. Logic supplies the
       language of assertion and proof. Set theory supplies a common universe
       of objects. Relations and functions express comparison and dependence.
       The natural, integer, and rational number systems are then constructed
       as successive solutions to limitations of the preceding system.
       Abstract and linear algebra isolate structural patterns shared by those
       examples. Real and complex analysis finally add completeness, limiting
       processes, and the rigidity of holomorphic functions.

       A displayed definition or result is meant to be read together with its
       context. Definitions fix conventions that may differ across books;
       theorem cards state mathematical content but do not replace proofs; and
       conjecture cards mark claims whose status is intentionally unresolved.
       The checker verifies the structure and internal references of the
       library, not the truth of the mathematics."
Id: "7bbe5cda-edfe-4c9a-8894-a3573ca752ac"
